# Both sides moved. Refused for the reason remote-ahead is, plus one more: the
# push would be rejected as a non-fast-forward, and the shortest way past that
# is the force-push this repository forbids. The repair is a merge, never a
# rebase, followed by rewriting `## Head` at the merge commit. Its own return
# code rather than remote-ahead's, so the refusal can say which of the two it
# is and carry both counts; the remedy is the same, the description is not.
#
# <branch or -> <remote or -> <own-remote-ref sha or -> <behind> <ahead> <rc> <compared ref or -> <text>
own-branch origin 9f8e7d6c5b4a392817065f4e3d2c1b0a98765432 1 3 5 origin/own-branch a diverged branch is refused
